// AC-3 tables from ATSC A/52 (the AC-3 standard): frame sizes (Table 5.18),
// channel counts per audio coding mode (Table 5.8), the bit allocation
// tables of section 7.2 (band edges, log-addition, hearing threshold, bap,
// decay/gain/floor parameters), rematrixing bands (7.5.2), quantiser sizes
// (Table 7.18) and the dequantised mantissa values for the grouped
// quantisers (Tables 7.19 to 7.23).
//
// Mantissas are kept as 24-bit fixed point numbers, as FFmpeg's decoder
// keeps them, so that our output agrees with FFmpeg's to rounding: a
// value v stands for v / 2^23 (the spec's −1…1 range is ±2^23).
//
// Author: Alexius Academia
// Date: 2026-10-25

// Words (16-bit) per syncframe for each frmsizecod, at 48, 44.1 and 32 kHz
